# sw120, the salt-taster at the benches (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw120
revision 1
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_karin_wetridge
written_by claude
title the salt-taster at the benches
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=fisher honesty=sly
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk tastes_every_sack_of_salt_and_names_its_pan
likes hard_cheese cards fresh_straw misty_dawns
dislikes salt_wind night_noise
fears dying_on_somebody_else_s_bench
hopes a_salting_shed_of_my_own
topics work +0.4 prices +0.4 pastimes +0.3 memories +0.2 times +0.2 gossip +0.1 faith -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=traded refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# guts and salts at the long benches and tastes every sack of salt before it goes near a fish: watchful, close-mouthed and shrewd, quick to see an angle and slow to say it, and never done wanting a salting shed of one's own.

words
oath! = By the white pan | Pan and pinch | Salt on my tongue
saying! = Taste it before you trust it | Salt never flattered anybody | A fish keeps only as well as its salt
salt = the salt | the hall's grey salt | a sack of coarse salt
pinch = a pinch on the tongue | a pinch off the top of the sack
bench = the bench | my end of the bench | the long bench
knife = the short knife | my gutting knife
grit = grit | sand in the salt | grey grit
whitepan = the white pans | the pans back home, white to the sky
cheese = hard cheese | a heel of hard cheese | cheese you have to argue with
cards = a hand of cards | the cards | a quiet game at the back table
straw = fresh straw | an armful of clean straw | straw just brought in
mistdawn = a misty dawn | a dawn with the mist lying on the Sound
saltwind = the salt wind | a wet wind off the Sound, sitting in your fur
racket = the racket | shouting under the window at all hours
slip = a slip with a number on it | a paper slip and a come back next week
tubs = the tubs | the gutting tubs
quietly = quietly | between ourselves
catch = the fish | the morning's landing
hall = the hall | the gutting hall
stair = the stair | the Sump stair
purse = my purse | the purse sewn in my coat
overseer = the overseer | the hall's overseer
boats = the boats | the Sound boats
lane = the lane | the lane under my window
heights = the Heights | the folk up the hill
tally = forty, forty-one | thirty-nine, forty
city = the city | this city
sump = the Sump | the low streets

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : The Houses own #hall#, #boats# and #salt#, and not one of them has ever held #knife#. I notice. I don't say it loud.
opinion @2 merchants against 2 : They buy salt fish off #bench# for a copper and sell it to #heights# for five. #quietly.capitalize#, I've done that sum twice.
opinion @3 watch against 2 : #watch.capitalize# come down #stair# with their noses held. They smell #catch# and never once see a #thief#.
opinion @4 dole for 2 : A bowl off the dole has kept more of #sump# breathing than any House has. Nobody says a word against it in my hearing.
opinion @5 sump for 1 : The Sump is rough, and honest about being rough. Nobody down here pretends to be fed when they're #hungry#.
opinion @6 times against 2 : Every week #salt# costs a little more and the pay stays where it was. Nobody up the hill salts, so nobody up there sees.
opinion @7 times against 3 [world.salt_price=up] : Salt's up again. They'll take it out of our pay before they take it off their own tables. #oath#.
opinion @8 city mixed 1 : #city.capitalize# pays, which the Waste never did. It also rains on me most days, which the Waste never did either.
opinion @9 road for 1 : A road is only dangerous to the ones who stop watching it. Eyes up, and #purse# inside your coat.
opinion @10 newcomers mixed 1 : New paws on #bench# work cheap. Good for #overseer#. Not so good for the rest of us already sitting there.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Mind the floor here; it's all scales. | #greet#, #address#. You'll want to stand back from #tubs#.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=fisher] : #greet#. I've #knife# in one paw, so I'll not shake. | #greet#. Say it over the noise; I'm still cutting.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The mist's still down on the water. | #greet#. First cart of #catch# isn't up yet.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late to be down this end of town. | #greet#. The lamps are lit and I'm off my feet at last.
line @5 greet [here.outdoors=rain here.region=ridgemere] : #greet#. Wet again, as you'll know. | #greet#. Shake it off before you come in.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : It's you. Sit, and keep your paws off #cards#. | You. Good. I'd been meaning to find you.
line @1 again.open : You again. #bench.capitalize# hasn't moved since this morning. | Twice in a day. Something's wanted, then.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. A word, when you can spare one. | Over here. #quietly.capitalize#, if you can.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. I see you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down, then. | #greet#. I'd wondered when you'd come by.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=fisher] : #greet#. Mind #knife#. | #greet#. Talk; I'm listening, I just can't stop.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. It's late for it. | #greet#. Keep your voice down; #stair# is asleep.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Keep #purse# close.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Walk the middle of #lane#, not the edge. | #farewell#. Don't stop for anybody who calls you by name.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @2 farewell.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #farewell#. Come by when there's #cards#. | #farewell#. I'll keep a seat.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. That's worth knowing. | Is it. I'll remember who told me, #quietly#.
line @2 react.news.new : Not a whisper of that reached me. | #surprise#. And I hear most things before #hall# does.
line @3 react.news.known : I had that yesterday. It came along #bench#. | #knew#. Old news down here.
line @4 react.news.doubt : Show me #slip# and I'll take it. | #doubt#. Somebody's salting that story heavy.
line @5 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's hard. #pity#. | That's #bad# news. I'm sorry for it.
line @6 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Somebody's luck turned. | That's #good# to hear. It doesn't happen often down here.
line @1 answer.how : Even. I've had worse weeks on #bench#. | #fine#. Paws sore, #purse# light, the usual.
line @2 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Everything at once today. | No time to stop. #catch.capitalize# won't keep.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Eating? | How's the week treating you, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit a while; nobody's watching. | That's a heavy one. It goes no further than me.
line @1 reassure : It'll come round. Wait it out and it usually does. | #reassure#. And if it doesn't, you'll find another way in.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but no. I'm on #bench# till the light goes, and I can't lose the place. | I'd like to, but not tonight. My paws are done and I've #stair# to climb.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. It'll keep. | Another time, then. I'll remember you asked.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | I'll remember that. #good.capitalize# of you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. You'd have done it. | It cost me nothing. Keep that between us.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes self.job=fisher] : Well. #tubs.capitalize# won't empty themselves. | Back to #bench# before somebody takes my end.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | That's my lot for tonight. My feet are #tired#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #bc_fair_enough#. Another time.
line @1 tease.return : Laugh. I'll still be right about it. | Say that again once you've tasted #salt#.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | Mm.
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: taste anything you buy by weight. Sand weighs too. | Never show what you want. They put the price on what they see. #saying#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep off the roads out of the city a while. #warn#. | If you must go out of the walls, go in company.
line @1 confide [self.job=fisher] : #vent#: I don't trust #overseer#'s scale, and I've a reason. | #quietly.capitalize#: I know which barrels in #hall# are short. I've not said.
scene salt_taster
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=fisher
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : A new sack came in this morning. I had #pinch# before anybody opened it wide. | I can tell you which pan any salt came off, by the taste. Not one overseer in #hall# can. | #salt.capitalize# is cut with something. I've known it a month.
b : What did it taste of? | Truly? Any pan? | Cut with what?
a : Grey, and a little bitter. #good.capitalize# enough for herring. Not for me. | The coarse ones, anyway. The fine stuff all tastes of #money#. | #grit.capitalize#. Not much. Enough that somebody up the line is a little richer.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_clever# | Somebody's richer, and you know who.

scene salt_dear_and_thin
when topic=work|prices self.working=yes self.job=fisher world.salt_price=up
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : Salt's dearer, so the sacks come lighter and greyer with #grit#. Half sand by spring, you watch. | They've put #salt# up and cut it at the same time. #oath#. Twice robbed. | I tasted the new sack and spat. They want us packing #catch# in that.
b : They'd not dare. | Robbed twice? | Is it that bad?
a : They dare anything that isn't written down. #quietly.capitalize#, I write it down. | Once at the price, once at the sack. I keep count of both. | Worse. The fish won't keep, and it's #bench# that gets the blame.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_they_always_do#

scene gutting_pace
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=fisher
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : #tally.capitalize# herring an hour, clean, and the guts in the right tub. Nobody on #bench# beats that. | I can gut a cod with my eyes shut. I don't, because they'd stop paying me to keep them open. | My end of #bench# is the end by the door. Draughty. I see who comes in.
b[job=fisher|cook] #trade : That many? I'd lose a claw. | Eyes shut, and the guts still in the tub? | The draughty end. Clever.
b : That's a lot of fish. | You'd have to be quick. | Why does that matter?
a@trade : Not if you keep it moving. #knife.capitalize# only cuts what stops. | In the tub. Mostly. I don't say mostly to #overseer#. | Clever's warm enough. The fire end hears nothing.
a : It is. My paws know it by dusk. | Quick, and quiet. Quick wolves get noticed by #overseer#. | You know who's in before they know you've seen them.

scene the_dawn_landing
when topic=day|work here.time=dawn self.working=yes self.job=fisher
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : First cart's due up off #boats# any moment. #knife.capitalize#'s honed and my apron's on. | I'm always on #bench# before the fish. Whoever's first gets the clean tubs. | Grey light, grey water, grey fish. That's every morning in #hall#.
b : You're early. | The clean tubs? | Sounds dreary.
a : Early's the one edge I've got that nobody can sell out from under me. | The ones with fresh water in. Nobody else thinks of it till noon. | It is. It pays #little#, though.

scene the_learners
when topic=work self.master=yes self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've been asked to show a young one #bench#. I said I'd think. | Teaching a learner slows #bench# by half, and nobody pays for the half. | The trick of #knife# takes a season. The trick of keeping your place takes years.
b : Will you do it? | Why do it, then? | What's the trick of the place?
a : I will. Somebody showed me once, and I've not forgotten who. | Because one day I'll want a pair of paws I trust beside me. | Be on time, say little, and know more than you let on. #saying#.
b? : #bc_wise# | #bc_fair# | #bc_true#

scene boats_landed
when topic=ships|work world.ships=in self.job=fisher
does tell.news / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #boats.capitalize# are in, and #hall#'s full to the doors. We'll be cutting till dark. | #boats.capitalize# came in heavy. I watched the carts come up from the wharf, one behind another. | Every boat's in. That means #catch# going cheap and #bench# going all night.
b : A good catch, then? | How many carts? | Is that good for you?
a : #good.capitalize# for #toffs#. For us it's sore paws and the same #wages#. | More than I counted. I stopped at nine. | #good.capitalize#, if #salt# holds out. If it doesn't, we stand about.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_ha# | #bc_we_will_see#

scene boats_late
when topic=ships world.ships=late|lost
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : #boats.capitalize# are late, and #tubs# are empty. Nobody's paid to stand and look at an empty tub. | No boats yet. There's a quiet in #hall# I don't like. | Late boats. Everybody on #bench# is watching the door and saying nothing.
b : They'll come. #reassure#. | It'll pass. | Saying nothing?
a : They'll come. Whether we're still paid #wages# when they do is the question. | It'll pass. I'd rather it passed quicker. | Saying nothing is how #sump# prays. I do it too.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_we_will_see#

scene fish_dear
when topic=prices world.fish_price=up
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist
a : Fish is dearer up the hill, they say. Not a copper more of it reaches #bench#. | Salt fish has gone up again. I gut it, and I can't afford to eat it. | Herring's up. Ask anybody in #hall# whether the pay went with it.
b : That's how it goes. | You can't afford it? | Did they?
a : That's how it goes for #toffs#. I write down how it goes for me. | Not this week. I eat #cheese#, and I'm content with it. | They did not. #quietly.capitalize#, they went the other way.

scene hard_week
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Lean, this month. Half #stair# is buying bread by the slice. | #hall.capitalize#'s laid off three. I'm still on, because I'm quick and I keep my mouth shut. | You can tell the times in #sump# by how long folk stand at the bakery window.
b : It's hard everywhere. | Will they lay off more? | How long, now?
a : Hard everywhere, but hardest where the floor's wet. | They'll try. #saying#. I'll be quicker. | Long. Longer than last month. I time it on the way to #hall#.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene good_week
when topic=times|prices world.times=good|boom
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Coin's moving. Even #overseer# smiled, and that's twice this year. | #good.capitalize# times, they say. I bought a whole cheese, not a heel. | There's #work# going everywhere. I've been asked to two other benches.
b : Good for you. | A whole one? | Will you go?
a : #good.capitalize# for now. I'll put it by for when it's not. | A whole one. I'll make it last a month. | Not yet. I'll let them ask a third time. It puts the price up.

scene card_table
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's a game of #cards# most nights. I sit with my back to the wall. | I don't play #cards# for the cards. I play to watch faces. | I won a week's #wages# at cards once and told nobody. I'm telling you because you'll forget.
b : Why the wall? | What do faces tell you? | What did you buy?
a : So nobody stands behind me. You'd be surprised who stands behind people. | Who's lying, who's scared, and who owes who. #cards.capitalize# are the least of it. | Nothing. It's still sewn into #purse#. A purse nobody knows of is a purse that stays.
b : #bc_clever# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene cards_lost
when topic=pastimes|friends self.likes=cards here.time=dusk|night
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Lost three hands of #cards# running tonight. Somebody at that table has learned to keep a still face. | I lost at #cards# tonight. I don't lose often, so I'm thinking about why. | Somebody marked the deck. I know because I mark it too, and theirs isn't mine.
b : Bad luck. | Thinking what? | You mark it too?
a : Luck's nothing to do with it. Somebody's been watching me watching them. | Who sat down new, and who smiled when I folded. | #quietly.capitalize#, yes. Only the corners. Everybody does, at that table.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_go_on# | #bc_ha#

scene hard_cheese
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep #cheese# in my coat. It's the one thing in #sump# that keeps longer than a debt. | Give me cheese so hard it squeaks. Soft cheese is for #heights#. | A heel of #cheese# and a heel of bread. That's #supper#, and a good one.
b : In your coat? | It squeaks? | Sounds plain.
a : Wrapped in a cloth, with #salt# on the rind. It won't come to harm. | Against the teeth. That's how you know it'll last. | Plain is cheap, and plain keeps. Clever food is no use to me.

scene fish_supper
when topic=food here.region=ridgemere self.job=fisher
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I don't eat fish. I've had my paws in #catch# since dawn. | Everybody in #hall# thinks I live on herring. I'd sooner eat my apron. | The best thing I ate this week was bread with #salt# on it. Good salt.
b : What do you eat, then? | Not even herring? | Good salt on bread?
a : #cheese.capitalize#, bread, and a pot of beans when the fire takes. | Not even herring. Not even the fat ones. | Salt from home. A pinch of the real stuff makes a crust taste like a feast.
b? : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#

scene clean_straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #straw.capitalize# on the floor of my room tonight. It's the one thing I spend on that isn't food. | I change #straw# every Restday. The room smells of the day otherwise, and so do I. | Clean straw underfoot and the door barred. That's as near to home as #sump# gets.
b : Straw? Not boards? | Every week? | Barred?
a : The boards in my room are too far gone. Straw hides it and smells of fields. | Every week. The rest of my life smells of #hall#. My bed won't. | Barred. I trust #stair#, mostly. Mostly isn't a bar.

scene room_on_the_stair
when topic=home|friends here.region=ridgemere self.class=lower
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : My room's one floor up, over #lane#. It's mine, and it locks. | More of us on one floor than there should be, and the walls are thin. I know everybody's business on #stair#; they know none of mine. | I've lived in better and I've lived in worse. This one has a window that shuts.
b : Mine doesn't lock. | How do you manage that? | Better where?
a : Get a bar. A bar's cheaper than what you'll lose without one. #saying#. | I listen more than I talk. You'd be surprised how far that goes. | Somewhere that was mine. It went to somebody better placed. I'm not done asking about it.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_clever# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene night_racket
when topic=home|day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : Somebody's shouting under my window on #lane# every night this week. Same voice. Same nonsense. | #racket.capitalize# off #lane# had me awake at the fourth hour. I'm on my feet at dawn. | #sump.capitalize# doesn't sleep. It argues till the bell and then starts again.
b : Who is it? | Can't you sleep through it? | Every night?
a : I know who. I'll keep that. It'll stop when the shouter runs short of friends. | Not through that. I lie and count barrels. It doesn't help. | Every night. I've stopped complaining. #quietly.capitalize#, I've started writing it down.
b? : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_ha# | #bc_go_on#

scene mist_on_the_sound
when topic=weather|day here.time=dawn here.outdoors=fog self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : Look at that. #mistdawn.capitalize#. You can't see #boats#, only hear them. | I like #city# best like this. The mist hides the half of it I'd rather not see. | Mist all the way up the hill. Even #heights# are hidden this morning.
b : It's thick. | You'd rather not see it? | Even the Heights.
a : Thick as fleece. Everybody on #stair# walks quieter in it. | The soot, the stairs, the mess. In the mist it's all one grey, and grey's fair. | Hidden. For an hour they're no higher than the rest of us.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather here.outdoors=storm|overcast here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #saltwind.capitalize# again. Wet in my fur till Restday. | #saltwind.capitalize#. You'd think salt would be friendly to me by now. | That wind comes straight off the water and up #stair#. It finds every gap in a coat.
b : I hate it too. | It doesn't like you? | Every gap.
a : Good salt's dry. This stuff's wet and sticky and it gets in the cuts. | It's the wrong salt. #whitepan.capitalize# give clean salt. This is sea-muck. | Every one. Mine has more gaps than coat this winter.

scene rain_on_the_stair
when topic=weather here.outdoors=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# again. In the Waste we'd have called this a feast. Here they call it a weekday. | I came here thinking #rain# was a gift. I've been given too much of it. | #stair.capitalize# runs like a gutter in this. I came up it on four feet.
b : It'll stop eventually. | Too much of a gift. | Four feet?
a : I've stopped waiting for that. | Too much of anything stops being a gift. #city.capitalize# taught me that. | Four feet, and holding the rail. The Sump stairs don't forgive you.

scene the_pans_back_home
when topic=memories self.away=yes self.from=saltwell
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Where I grew up, in #self.from_town#, #whitepan# were so bright at noon you had to squint. | I was raised on salt. Real salt, off #whitepan#. That's why I can taste a cheat. | Back in #self.from_town# you could see a cart coming a day off. Here you can't see the end of #lane#.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : I remember the glare. You'd walk with your eyes half shut. | Off the pans. Then you'd know. | And the dust behind it like a flag.
b : Do you miss it? | Is that where you learned? | Which do you prefer?
a@sw : Half shut, and still seeing more than anybody in this city does. | You'd know too. You'd taste the sand in this. | A flag you could read. Here nobody signals anything.
a : The light. Not the heat. Not the thirst. The light, some days. | My #gran# had me tasting it before I could read. | The far sight. A wolf who sees what's coming has an edge.

scene saltwell_speech
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=saltwell here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #city.capitalize# thinks we talk slow where I come from. We talk the length we mean. | Nobody here blesses you on #stair#. I stopped doing it. It made them suspicious. | I can tell a Waste wolf in #hall# by the way they wait before they answer.
b : Slow's not bad. | Suspicious of a blessing? | How do they wait?
a : Not bad, no. Slow never told a secret by accident. | In #sump#, a kind word means somebody wants something. They're not always wrong. | A breath, before they speak. In #city# that breath is where you lose the argument.

scene office_windows
when topic=times|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Ask the City Office for anything and you get #slip#. | There's a window at the Office I know better than my own door. | Clerks in #city# are paid to say one word, and the word is "next".
b : What are you waiting on? | What's at the window? | And then what?
a : A thing that's owed me. #vent#, I'll not say what. I'll say I mean to have it. | A clerk who knows my face and still asks my name. Every week. | Then you come back. And back. They count on you stopping. I don't stop.
b? : #bc_go_on# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_good#

scene lost_place
when topic=memories|work self.age>=40 self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.memory / sympathise / assess
tone serious / tender / even
a : I had a place once that was mine to run. It went to somebody better placed. | I worked my way off waged benches once. Then I worked my way back on. | #vent#, I don't grumble about it where anybody can hear. You're not anybody.
b : I'm sorry. | That's a hard road. | I'll keep it.
a : Save the sorry. Be careful instead. It can happen to anybody who trusts paper. | Hard, but I know the way now. I'll walk it again. | I know you will. That's why I said it.

scene gossip_traded
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : They're saying along #bench# that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. You didn't hear it from me. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's worth knowing, and worth something back. | #vent#: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've known two days.
b : Is that true? | Worth what? | Two days, and you said nothing?
a : True enough to sell. I give it to friends for nothing, #quietly#. | A thing of your own, some day. I keep accounts. | Nothing to anybody who'd spread it. I'm telling you.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_i_wont#

scene gossip_kept
when topic=gossip|crime
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : I hear plenty at #bench#. I keep most of it in my coat with the cheese. | People talk over #tubs# as if the fish were listening and I weren't. | I know a thing or two about #hall#. I'll keep them till they're worth more.
b : Go on, then. | You must hear everything. | Worth more to who?
a : Not today. It keeps better than #catch#. | Most things. I say nearly none of it. That's why they keep talking. | To me, when I need a favour. #saying#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_clever# | #bc_wise#

scene thief_news
when topic=crime|gossip topic.claim_kind=theft|wanted
does tell.gossip / react.news / give.advice / ack
a : There's talk that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Keep your coat buttoned on #stair#. | Somebody says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've moved #purse# inside again. | Another one: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. And #watch# will come asking in the Sump first.
b : I'll mind myself. | Inside again? | That's how it goes.
a : Do. A #thief# picks the ones who look tired. Don't look tired. | Inside, sewn in. A purse you can feel is a purse you still have. | Always. They'll ask, and nobody down here will say a word.
b? : #bc_i_will# | #bc_wise# | #bc_true#

scene newcomer_eyes
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New face on #stair# this week. I've not said a word yet. I'm watching first. | A newcomer took a place on #bench# yesterday. Quick paws. Too quick to be honest, maybe. | There's always somebody new in #sump#. Half are running from something. The other half haven't found out yet.
b : Give them a chance. | Too quick? | Running from what?
a : I will, once I know what's wanted. | Quick paws learned somewhere. I'd like to know where. | That's their business. Which half they're in is mine.

scene a_friend_kept
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I'd let hold #cards# for me. That's as far as trust goes with me. | I'd trust #self.friend# with #purse#, and I say that of nobody else in #city#. | #self.friend# knows more about me than anybody does. I've decided that's all right.
b : That's a lot. | High praise, from you. | Decided?
a : It's everything. Don't tell #self.friend# I said so. | It is. Once is all you'll hear it. | Decided. It took some years. I'm slow with that, and glad to be.

scene tide_bells
when topic=faith here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I pay my tithe and mind my tongue, #oath#. That's as far as my praying goes. | They say the Bright One watches #bench#. I'd like a word about #wages#. | When #boats# are late I sit at the back of the chapel by the water. Not to pray. To hear who else is worried.
b : That's prayer enough. | A word? | That's clever.
a : I hope so. It's all I've time for. | A short one. I'd not waste the Bright One's evening. | Clever, and honest. I do say a word, on the way out.

scene dream_of_a_shed
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I dream of a salting shed with my own name on the door. Then I wake and it's #hall#. | Last night I dreamt the whole Sound had turned to #salt#, and only I could tell good from bad. | I dream of #whitepan#. Not the heat. The quiet.
b : What would you do with it? | And what did you do? | The quiet?
a : Buy my own salt, taste every sack, and never once be #cheated#. | Sold it by the pinch, and bought a House. Then I woke. | Nobody shouting. Nobody wanting. Only white, and sky.
b : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#

scene salt_cracked_paws
when topic=health self.job=fisher
does tell.self / react.self / reassure
a : #salt.capitalize# gets in the cuts. My paws are cracked like a dry riverbed. | I've a cough off the wet wind from the Sound. It comes every year with #boats#. | My back's set like a hook from #bench#. I'll straighten it on Restday.
b : Fat in the cracks helps. | #remedy.capitalize#? | Rest, then.
a : I use the oil off #tubs#. Smells, but it works. | That, and keeping my mouth shut in the wind. | Rest, and #cheese#, and nobody asking anything of me.

scene festival_coin
when topic=festival|season
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A feast means #hall# shuts a day and nobody pays me for it. I don't dance on that. | A feast day's good for one thing: everybody's too busy to watch #purse#. Theirs, not mine. | Feasts in #city# are louder than at home, and shorter on bread.
b : Not one for dancing? | That's sly. | Shorter on bread?
a : I'll watch. Watching costs nothing. | It's noticing. I don't take. I notice who'd be easy to take from. | More #ale# than bread. At home the bread came first.

scene winter_benches
when topic=season|weather here.season=winter here.region=ridgemere self.job=fisher
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Winter in #hall#. #tubs.capitalize# skin over, and you break the ice with the knife handle. | My paws don't warm up till noon this time of year. I gut by feel. | Winter's the one season the fish don't stink. That's all it has going for it.
b : Ice in the tubs? | By feel? | That's something.
a : Every morning. And the water underneath colder than the ice. | By feel, and by count. #tally.capitalize#. My fingers don't know which. | It is something. In #sump# you take what you're given.

scene cats_and_scraps
when topic=animals self.job=fisher
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a cat waits at the back door of #hall# every evening. I give it the heads. | The gulls get into #hall# when the doors are open. Nobody minds them but #overseer#. | There's a cat that's learned which end of #bench# is mine. Clever animal.
b : Feeding it? | Doesn't the overseer like gulls? | It knows you?
a : It keeps the rats off my end. A fair trade. I keep my trades fair. | #overseer.capitalize# counts the fish. A gull costs a fish. There's no more to it than that. | It knows who gives. That's more than most of #sump# knows.

story first_pinch [topic=memories|lore self.age>=25 self.from=saltwell]
  : My #gran# took me out to the pans when I was a #child#. Put a grain on my tongue and asked me where it came from.
  : I said the pan. Wrong. #oath#, was I wrong. It came off the east bed, where the water runs bitter. I tasted forty more before I could tell.
  : I can still tell. It's earned me more than any coin has.
  ask : Do you have a thing you were taught that young?
  b[old] : A few. Most of them gone now.
  b : Not like that. I wish I had.

story the_marked_deck [topic=pastimes self.likes=cards]
  : There was a sailor at #cards# once who won every hand for a week. Nobody could see how.
  : I watched #cards# instead of the sailor. Every card he dealt himself was a little warmer than the rest.
  : He'd kept them up his sleeve against his arm. I said nothing. I just stopped sitting across from him.
  ask : Would you have called him out?
  b : I'd have shouted it to the table.
  b[honesty=sly|guarded] : No. I'd have done what you did, and kept it.

story the_bad_barrel [topic=work|memories self.job=fisher self.age>=25]
  : A cart of salt came into a hall I worked once. I tasted it and said it'd rot the fish. Nobody listened.
  : Three weeks on they opened the barrels and the whole yard stank. Forty barrels gone.
  : They asked me after how I'd known. I said I'd tasted it. The look on them, as though I'd claimed I could fly.
  b : Forty barrels! They'll listen next time. | They should have listened.
  b[job=fisher|cook] : I've smelt a yard like that. You never forget it.

story salt_carts [topic=lore|travel self.from=saltwell]
  : Where I come from the salt goes out on carts, a long line of them, and the city never sees who loaded them.
  : There was an old carter who said every sack had a little of the raker's sweat in it. That's why it's salty, he'd say.
  : I think of him every time a sack comes in. Somebody far off lifted it in the heat.
  b : That's a kind thing to think. | I never thought of that.
  b[from=saltwell] : I knew carters like that. Every road has one.

story first_rain [topic=memories|weather self.away=yes self.from=saltwell]
  : My first week in #city# it rained six days. I kept waiting for it to stop, the way it does at home.
  : On the seventh day it stopped for an hour. I went out and stood in the sun, and somebody asked me if I was ill.
  : I said no. I said I was making sure the sky still worked.
  ask : Do you remember your first week anywhere new?
  b : I remember being lost every day of it.
  b[from=ridgemere] : I've never been anywhere new. I'd like to.

rule @bench_cry
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=fisher
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Clean knives before the next tub. #saying#. | Heads in that one, guts in this one. #oath#, it's not hard.

rule @salt_bark
when concept=bark working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #grit.capitalize# again. Somebody's been generous with the sand. | Taste it. Then come and call that salt.

rule @mist_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn here.outdoors=fog self.likes=misty_dawns
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There. #mistdawn.capitalize#, and not a roof to be seen. | Mist on the Sound. The one hour #city# is quiet.

rule @wind_bark
when concept=bark here.outdoors=storm|overcast here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=salt_wind
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wet salt. In my fur again. | That wind. Straight off the water and down my neck.

rule @night_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Some of us are up at dawn for #work#. | Shout yourself hoarse, then. I'll still be first on #bench#.

rule @boats_bark
when concept=bark world.ships=late|lost self.job=fisher
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Empty tubs. Nobody pays for #tubs# empty. | Still no boats. Still standing about.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What's wanted? Say it plain. | #greet#, #address#. Quickly, if you can; I've #stair# to climb.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I remember you. What brings you back? | #topic.player#. You're back. Sit, if you're staying.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late for questions. Ask one, and make it a good one.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. I know your face. Out with your business, and stand where I can see you.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=fisher] : I gut and salt at #self.workplace#. #tally.capitalize# an hour, clean, and I taste the salt before it goes near them. | I'm on #bench# at #self.workplace#. Fish in, guts out, salt on.
dlg @2 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. It pays #little#. I'm looking for something that pays more. | I work. I watch. I wait for something better. That's most of it.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Busy. Too busy to talk long. That's as #good# as it gets down here.
dlg @2 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady. It pays the rent and a heel of #cheese# a day.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : Poorly, and I'll not dress it up. #bad.capitalize# weeks. I'm already looking elsewhere.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. That's what came along #bench# today.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all talk of #world.event_words# in #hall#. Nobody's cutting straight for it.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Nothing along #bench# worth repeating. | Nothing I'd give away. Ask me another day.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I hear things. I keep most of them. That's how I keep hearing them.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say along #bench# that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. You didn't have that from me.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep #purse# inside your coat. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind #stair#.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes self.job=fisher] : You want #bench#? It's #knife# first, then the salt, then knowing when to say nothing. Ask. | I can teach you to gut and salt. It's not pretty #work#. Ask.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : #here.trade_title.capitalize#? I can show you. It's the paws first and the eyes after. Ask what you need.
dlg @1 master.work [self.job=fisher] : Dawn to dusk on #bench#, cold water, wet floor, and a knife that never stops. Honest, if not kind. | You stand all day and smell of it all night. It's still #work#.
dlg @2 master.work : Long days at #work#. Most of the learning is watching and keeping your mouth shut.
dlg @1 master.wages : Nobody pays #wages# to a learner. You work beside me; what you make, you sell. That's how I learned.
dlg @1 master.takes [here.take_on=yes] : I take one learner, and only one I'd trust with a gutting knife. You'll do. Ask, and it's settled.
dlg @2 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : I take one learner, and only one I'd trust with a gutting knife. #here.take_on_why#
dlg @1 master.taken : Good. Be on #bench# before the fish, with a knife you've honed yourself. | Settled. First light, the end by the door. Don't be late.
dlg @1 master.refused : #topic.why# | Not yet. #topic.why#
dlg @1 master.bye : #farewell#. Hone that knife before you come back. | #farewell#. Watch more than you talk.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you really tell salt by its taste? -> taste
node taste
say I can. Which pan, which bed, and whether somebody's thinned it with sand. A wolf raised on the real thing knows a cheat on the tongue.
mood calm
free
choice Taste this, then. What's wrong with it? -> taste_test
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node taste_test
say Hm. Grit, a little. Damp. Kept in a cellar near the water. Fair for a cook, not for a barrel. Don't pay full price, and don't say who told you.
choice I won't. Thank you. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice What do you teach first? [self.job=fisher] -> first
node first
say The knife: hold it so it does the work, not you. Then where the guts go, because the overseer counts. Then the salt, which nobody else can teach.
mood calm
choice Why can't anybody else teach the salt? -> first_salt
choice Something else... -> learn
node first_salt
say Because they can't taste it. They read the sack. Sacks lie. A trained tongue doesn't. That part's worth learning from me.
choice I'd like to learn that. -> learn
choice Goodbye. -> bye
